To characterize the spatial extent of the merger sample, we estimated the total angular sky area over which the 3,166 galaxy mergers are distributed. This effective footprint was computed by dividing the sky into finer bins in right ascension and declination and summing up the area of all the spatial bins that contained at least one merger. The contribution of each bin was corrected for spherical projection by weighting with cos($\delta$), where $\delta$ is the central declination of the bin. This produced an estimated sky coverage of approximately \(6190~\mathrm{deg}^2\), which was used for surface density estimates and association probability calculations. Figure~\ref{fig:sky_distribution} shows the sky distribution in equatorial coordinates using an Aitoff projection.
