\subsection{ Sensitivity to Parameters }
We conduct a parameter sensitivity analysis on the LaSOT dataset to examine the robustness of our tracker HiM2SAM-L under different settings.
Figure~\ref{fig:param_sensitivity} presents the evaluation results for three key parameters:
(1) the number of frames used by the point tracker for temporal propagation;
(2) the IoU threshold $\tau$ used during coarse motion estimation to decide whether a fine motion estimation is needed (triggered when the IoU falls below $\tau$);
and (3) different combinations of frame intervals for long-term memory (LM) and short-term memory (SM).
We find that while the tracker maintains overall stability, careful tuning of $\tau$ and memory intervals can yield marginal improvements in AUC.

