\begin{abstract}
\noindent 
It is observed that on a compact  almost complex Calabi-Yau with torsion (ACYT) 6-manifold with co-closed Lee form the curvature of the torsion connection is an $SU(3)$-instanton if and only if the torsion is parallel with respect to the torsion connection. The same conclusion holds for any 
(non necessarily compact)
balanced ACYT 6-manifold. In particular, on a CYT 6-manifold the Strominger-Bismut connection is 
an $SU(3)$-instanton if and only if the torsion is parallel with respect to the Strominger-Bismut connection provided either the CYT 6-manifold  is compact with co-closed Lee form or it is a balanced CYT 6-manifold.

\medskip

Keywords: torsion connection, $SU(3)$ holonomy, almost Calabi-Yau with torsion $SU(3)$-instanton


\medskip

AMS MSC2020: 53C55, 53C21, 53C29, 53Z05
\end{abstract}

