\section{Conclusion and Discussion}\label{Conclussions_study_findings}

We introduced an adaptive MCMC modeling technique for lifetime data, utilizing a concise set of default prior distributions. This approach enables precise characterization of key survival time measures, such as the mean remaining lifetime, particularly for patients with terminal illnesses like prostate cancer. Our findings show that prior selection depends on sample size and hazard rate patterns. However, our algorithm adaptively identifies the most effective shape and scale prior combinations for any given dataset.

