{\bf(ii)} Regarding the desingularization diagram 
$$\xymatrix{{\widetilde{Z'}_{0}}\ar@/^1pc/[rr]^{\tilde{i'}_{0}}\ar@{^{(}->}[r]_{\sigma}\ar[rd]_{\phi'_{0}}&{\widetilde{Z}}_{0}\ar@{^{(}->}[r]_{\tilde{i}_{0}}\ar[d]^{\phi_{0}}&\widetilde{Z}\ar[d]^{\phi}\\
&Z_{0}\ar@{^{(}->}[r]^{{i}_{0}}&Z}$$
we can propose another method to prove the assertion about the depth of the sheaf ${\mathcal L}^{m}_{Z}$. Using relative duality for a proper morphism, we easily obtain the commutative diagrams 
$$\xymatrix{{i_{0}}_{*}{\rm I}\!{\rm R}{{\phi'_{0}}_{*}}\omega^{m-1}_{\widetilde{Z}'_{0}}\eq[d]\eq[r]&
{\rm I}\!{\rm R}{\phi_{*}}{\rm R}{\mathcal H}om(\tilde{i'_{0}}_{*}{{\mathcal O}_{\widetilde{Z'}_{\!\!0}}}, \Omega^{m}_{\widetilde{Z}})[1]\eq[r]\ar[rd]_{u}&{\rm I}\!{\rm R}{\mathcal H}om({i_{0}}_{*}{\rm I}\!{\rm R}{{\phi'_{0}}_{*}}{\mathcal O}_{\widetilde{Z'_{0}}}, \omega^{m}_{Z})[1]\\
{i_{0}}_{*}{\mathcal L}^{m-1}_{Z_0}\ar[rr]&&{\rm I}\!{\rm R}{\mathcal H}om({i_{0}}_{*}{\rm I}\!{\rm R}{{\phi'_{0}}_{*}}{{\mathcal O}_{\widetilde{Z'_{0}}}}, {\mathcal L}^{m}_{Z})[1]\ar[u]_{v}} $$
and similarly, 
$$\xymatrix{{i_{0}}_{*}{\rm I}\!{\rm R}{\phi_{0}}_{*}\omega^{m-1}_{\widetilde{Z_{0}}}\eq[r]&{\rm I}\!{\rm R}\phi_{*}{\rm R}{\mathcal H}om({\tilde{i_{0}}_{*}}{\mathcal O}_{\widetilde{Z}_{0}}, \Omega^{m}_{\widetilde Z})[1]\eq[r]\ar[rd]&{\rm I}\!{\rm R}{\mathcal H}om({i_{0}}_{*}{\rm I}\!{\rm R}{\phi_{0}}_{*}{\mathcal O}_{\widetilde{Z}_{0}}, \omega^{m}_{Z})[1]\\
&&{\rm I}\!{\rm R}{\mathcal H}om({i_{0}}_{*}{\rm I}\!{\rm R}{\phi_{*}}{\mathcal O}_{\widetilde{Z_{0}}}, {\mathcal L}^{m}_{Z})[1]\ar[u]} $$
The spectral sequences 
$${\rm E}^{i,j}_{2}:={\mathcal Ext}^{i}({\mathcal H}^{j}({i_{0}}_{*}{\rm I}\!{\rm R}{\phi'_{0}}_{*}{\mathcal O}_{\widetilde{Z}'_{0}}), \omega^{m}_{Z})\Longrightarrow\, {\mathcal Ext}^{i-j}({i_{0}}_{*}{\rm I}\!{\rm R}{\phi'_{0}}_{*}{\mathcal O}_{\widetilde{Z}'_{0}}, \omega^{m}_{Z})$$
$${\rm E}'^{i,j}_{2}:={\rm I}\!{\rm R}^{i}\phi_{*}{\mathcal Ext}^{j}(\tilde{i'_{0}}_{*}{\mathcal O}_{\widetilde{Z}'_{0}}, \Omega^{m}_{\widetilde Z})\Longrightarrow\, {\mathcal Ext}^{i+j}({i_{0}}_{*}{\rm I}\!{\rm R}{\phi'_{0}}_{*}{\mathcal O}_{\widetilde{Z}'_{0}}, \omega^{m}_{Z})$$
and their analogues for $\widetilde{Z}_{0}$, satisfy 
$${\rm E}'^{i,j}_{2}=0\,\,\forall\,(i,j)\not=(0,1),\,\,{\rm E}^{1,0}_{2}\simeq{\mathcal Ext}^{1}({i_{0}}_{*}{\rm I}\!{\rm R}{\phi'_{0}}_{*}{\mathcal O}_{\widetilde{Z}'_{0}}, \omega^{m}_{Z})$$
since ${\rm I}\!{\rm R}^{1}\phi_{*}{\mathcal O}_{\widetilde{Z}'_{0}}$ being torsion, ${\rm E}^{0,1}_{2}=0$ (similarly for $\widetilde{Z}_{0}$). The exact sequence of low-degree terms then gives us the isomorphisms 
$${i_{0}}_{*}{\mathcal L}^{m-1}_{Z_0}\simeq \phi_{*}{\mathcal Ext}^{1}(\tilde{i'_{0}}_{*}{\mathcal O}_{\widetilde{Z}'_{0}}, \Omega^{m}_{\widetilde Z})\simeq {\mathcal Ext}^{1}({i_{0}}_{*}{\phi'_{0}}_{*}{\mathcal O}_{\widetilde{Z}'_{0}}, \omega^{m}_{Z})\simeq {\mathcal Ext}^{1}({i_{0}}_{*}{\rm I}\!{\rm R}{\phi'_{0}}_{*}{\mathcal O}_{\widetilde{Z}'_{0}}, \omega^{m}_{Z})$$
and 
$${i_{0}}_{*}{\phi_{0}}_{*}{\omega}^{m-1}_{\widetilde{Z}_0}\simeq \phi_{*}{\mathcal Ext}^{1}(\tilde{i_{0}}_{*}{\mathcal O}_{\widetilde{Z}_{0}}, \Omega^{m}_{\widetilde Z})\simeq {\mathcal Ext}^{1}({i_{0}}_{*}{\phi_{0}}_{*}{\mathcal O}_{\widetilde{Z}_{0}}, \omega^{m}_{Z})\simeq {\mathcal Ext}^{1}({i_{0}}_{*}{\rm I}\!{\rm R}{\phi_{0}}_{*}{\mathcal O}_{\widetilde{Z}_{0}}, \omega^{m}_{Z}) $$
Since $\widetilde{Z}_{0}$ and $\widetilde{Z}'_{0}$ are Gorenstein, the direct image morphism by the embedding $\sigma:\widetilde{Z}'_{0}\into \widetilde{Z}_{0}$ defined at the level of dualizing complexes 
$$\sigma_{*}{\Omega}^{m-1}_{\widetilde{Z}'_0}\rightarrow {\omega}^{m-1}_{\widetilde{Z}_0}$$
induces a natural morphism 
$$\sigma_{*}{\mathcal O}_{\widetilde{Z}'_0}\rightarrow {\mathcal O}_{\widetilde{Z}_0}$$
which can, in fact, be defined directly by reducing to the case where $\widetilde{Z}'_{0}$ is an irreducible component of $\widetilde{Z}_{0}$. Indeed, if ${\mathcal I}$ is the defining ideal of $\widetilde{Z}'_{0}$ in $\widetilde{Z}_{0}$ such that $\sigma_{*}{\mathcal O}_{{\widetilde{Z}'_{0}}}={\mathcal O}_{\widetilde{Z}_{0}}/{\mathcal I}$, the short exact sequence 
$$\xymatrix{0\ar[r]&{\mathcal I}\ar[r]&{\mathcal O}_{\widetilde{Z}_{0}}\ar[r]_{\beta}&\ar@/_1pc/[l]^{\alpha}{\mathcal O}_{\widetilde{Z}_{0}}/{\mathcal I}\ar[r]&0}$$
and naturally $\alpha\circ \beta\in {\mathcal H}om({\mathcal O}_{\widetilde{Z}_{0}}, {\mathcal O}_{\widetilde{Z}_{0}})$ is annihilated by ${\mathcal I}$.\vspace{2mm}

\noindent We thus construct a non-trivial morphism 
$${\phi_{0}}_{*}{\omega}^{m-1}_{\widetilde{Z}_0}\rightarrow {\mathcal L}^{m-1}_{Z_0}$$
which is necessarily injective since generically bijective and the sheaves are torsion-free. But since ${i_{0}}_{*}{\phi_{0}}_{*}{\omega}^{m-1}_{\widetilde{Z}_0}\simeq {\mathcal L}^{m}_{Z_0}/f{\mathcal L}^{m}_{Z_0}$, we have a natural injection of ${\mathcal L}^{m}_{Z_0}/f{\mathcal L}^{m}_{Z_0}$ into ${i_{0}}_{*}{\mathcal L}^{m-1}_{Z_0}$. Hence, finally, the isomorphisms 
$${i_{0}}_{*}{\mathcal L}^{m-1}_{Z_0}\simeq {\mathcal L}^{m}_{Z_0}/f{\mathcal L}^{m}_{Z_0}\simeq \simeq {\mathcal E}xt^{1}({i_{0}}_{*}{\mathcal O}_{Z_0}, {\mathcal L}^{m}_{Z})$$





