\subsection{Data structures \label{sec:datastruct}}

To preserve the modularity of the Matlab functions, we have standardized the input, output and data structures. If new modules are developed for community use, new developers must use the same formatting. Each module has three inputs, a structure containing file parameters, a structure containing module parameters, and a verbose flag. The file parameters structure includes information used to find input files and save output files, represented by green, yellow, and blue boxes in Fig.~\ref{fig:overview}. Each module has its own module parameter structure containing user set parameters needed to run the module. Verbose is a Boolean field that shows the user figures mid-use for quality control. The output of each function is a \textsc{true/false} flag to indicate successful completion of the current module along with module specific outputs saved in the designated directory.



